1
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:29,460
Back in high school.

2
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:36,320
Naoya, arriving at the computer lab,
looked more exhausted by the day.

3
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:57,780
Naoya.

4
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:08,320
Takaaki... is it time?

5
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:10,540
Have you been getting any sleep lately?

6
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:13,880
That wasn't a nap.
You practically passed out.

7
00:01:14,030 --> 00:01:15,500
You're clearly overworked.

8
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:16,780
Shut up.

9
00:01:17,030 --> 00:01:18,820
Don't boss me around.

10
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:38,240
I'm going to make that man
acknowledge me, no matter what.

11
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,560
I see.

12
00:01:50,190 --> 00:01:53,820
It's not about living up to
your father's expectations.

13
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:57,300
It's about making him acknowledge you.

14
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,550
Hey, let's keep going.

15
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:02,720
Got it.

16
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:10,880
I ran into my father
at my part-time job.

17
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:14,510
I wondered where you'd been hiding.

18
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:16,089
To think you'd be in a place like this.

19
00:02:16,090 --> 00:02:18,880
Doing bottom-feeder work
that even a monkey could do.

20
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,240
Did something happen?

21
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:26,060
I messed up at work.

22
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:28,340
Messed up?

23
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:32,020
Hey, hold me.

24
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:35,520
You can do whatever you want.

25
00:02:37,650 --> 00:02:40,609
While being dragged down
into the abyss by his family,

26
00:02:40,633 --> 00:02:43,656
Naoya still fought back with all
his might. His strength and his pain...

27
00:02:44,666 --> 00:02:47,006
inextricably drew me to him.

28
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Servant Prince (Episode 4)

29
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,300
What a pathetic guy.

30
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:53,420
I like you, Naoya.

31
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:58,000
Instead of always focusing
on what you don't have,

32
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:01,760
you should cherish what
you do have right now.

33
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:03,470
Takaaki.

34
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,200
I love you.

35
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:17,730
Delicious.

36
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:44,300
Yes.

37
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,400
That's all for now.

38
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:55,320
Excuse me.

39
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:00,460
President.

40
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:05,740
We just received notice from Goto Construction
that they won't be renewing their contract.

41
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:07,820
I see.

42
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:12,410
It doesn't matter.

43
00:06:16,850 --> 00:06:17,860
I'll take my leave then.

44
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:37,940
So they really did cancel the contract.

45
00:06:49,010 --> 00:06:50,010
Good morning.

46
00:06:52,990 --> 00:06:54,050
Goto-kun.

47
00:06:56,410 --> 00:06:57,410
I'm so glad.

48
00:06:57,950 --> 00:06:59,010
You decided to come.

49
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:05,970
That was the first time I've ever
talked about my situation like that.

50
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:07,630
Yeah.

51
00:07:08,650 --> 00:07:09,880
So I came.

52
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:17,630
The least I can do is not run away from the
people who are willing to look at who I am now.

53
00:07:19,690 --> 00:07:22,499
- Good morning.
- Good morning, Goto-kun.

54
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,500
Morning.

55
00:07:23,650 --> 00:07:25,020
- Good morning.
- Morning.

56
00:07:25,270 --> 00:07:26,270
Good morning.

57
00:07:26,690 --> 00:07:27,690
I get it now.

58
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:30,530
I didn't want to become strong.

59
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:41,530
I just wanted to live as myself.

60
00:07:41,570 --> 00:07:43,600
Here is your Americano and Vienna coffee.

61
00:07:45,730 --> 00:07:47,960
Goto-kun is doing great.

62
00:07:48,390 --> 00:07:50,010
The shop has really livened up.

63
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:51,760
It sure has.

64
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:54,630
Enjoy.

65
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:57,680
Welcome.

66
00:08:01,670 --> 00:08:02,670
Yuma...

67
00:08:03,850 --> 00:08:05,020
It's been a while.

68
00:08:06,510 --> 00:08:07,549
Brother.

69
00:08:07,550 --> 00:08:09,110
Huh? Is he your brother?

70
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:12,030
Not again.

71
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:23,750
Alright.

72
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Take us to our table.

73
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:27,380
You work here, right?

74
00:08:35,830 --> 00:08:36,950
Want to switch with me?

75
00:08:37,370 --> 00:08:38,370
Goto-kun.

76
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,440
I'm fine.

77
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,649
Right this way.

78
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:48,650
Please have a seat here.

79
00:08:58,170 --> 00:08:59,670
Here are your appetizers.

80
00:09:00,110 --> 00:09:05,430
From the right, we have salmon carpaccio, pâté
de campagne, and prosciutto cheese bruschetta.

81
00:09:06,090 --> 00:09:07,750
Enjoy your meal.

82
00:09:09,070 --> 00:09:10,070
Have a wonderful meal.

83
00:09:11,830 --> 00:09:13,550
When exactly are you planning to come back?

84
00:09:14,170 --> 00:09:16,470
Come back?

85
00:09:16,570 --> 00:09:17,570
Don't play dumb.

86
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:19,640
Huh?

87
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:24,060
You're always defying Dad.

88
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:29,250
And now you're working in a place like
this. Are you just doing this to mock us?

89
00:09:29,810 --> 00:09:30,940
Defying him?

90
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,380
Me?

91
00:09:36,070 --> 00:09:38,300
I have never... defied him.

92
00:09:39,490 --> 00:09:40,829
Are you serious?

93
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:42,449
Stop it, everyone is looking.

94
00:09:42,450 --> 00:09:43,660
You shut up.

95
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:46,140
Who do you think you are?

96
00:09:47,210 --> 00:09:48,540
You've always been like this...

97
00:09:48,830 --> 00:09:51,710
Flawlessly solving every
impossible task Dad threw at you,

98
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,310
without ever bowing your head.

99
00:09:55,390 --> 00:09:59,570
And you even stayed at that company
everyone said wouldn't last six months.

100
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:02,420
You stubbornly held on for
three whole years for nothing.

101
00:10:04,070 --> 00:10:07,510
If you had just said, 'I can't do it, '

102
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:09,070
and bowed your head to Dad,

103
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:11,360
he would have given you
any position you wanted.

104
00:10:16,930 --> 00:10:18,630
I never...

105
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:21,470
even thought about that.

106
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:30,270
Come back.

107
00:10:38,210 --> 00:10:40,040
I can't handle it all by myself anymore.

108
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:50,940
I'm sorry.

109
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,650
I'm not going back.

110
00:11:00,070 --> 00:11:01,030
Let's go.

111
00:11:01,031 --> 00:11:02,389
Hey, wait a minute.

112
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:03,390
Yuma.

113
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:08,320
Don't push yourself too hard.

114
00:11:14,390 --> 00:11:16,269
Wait.
Yuma, are you okay?

115
00:11:16,270 --> 00:11:17,469
Not at all.

116
00:11:17,470 --> 00:11:18,470
Huh?

117
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:21,930
Damn it...

118
00:11:22,510 --> 00:11:23,850
What the hell.

119
00:11:24,650 --> 00:11:25,650
Yuma.

120
00:11:36,210 --> 00:11:38,690
I'm really sorry for causing a scene
in the restaurant earlier.

121
00:11:40,250 --> 00:11:41,250
Here.

122
00:11:42,490 --> 00:11:45,510
The chef prepared some fruit jelly.

123
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:47,470
Could you hand these out to the tables?

124
00:11:53,470 --> 00:11:54,470
Sure.

125
00:12:00,550 --> 00:12:01,910
It's so good, right?

126
00:12:03,830 --> 00:12:05,049
I apologize for the disturbance earlier.

127
00:12:05,050 --> 00:12:06,549
Oh, no worries.

128
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:08,019
This is on the house.

129
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:08,930
Are you sure?

130
00:12:08,931 --> 00:12:10,599
- Yes.
- It looks delicious.

131
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:13,189
- So cute.
- Thank you.

132
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:15,980
- We're so lucky.
- Don't be rude.

133
00:12:16,510 --> 00:12:19,110
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

134
00:12:20,470 --> 00:12:22,450
Goto-san, let me help too.

135
00:12:22,850 --> 00:12:23,850
Thanks.

136
00:12:32,910 --> 00:12:38,190
In the past, to meet all
of my father's demands,

137
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:45,030
even having clones of myself
wouldn't have been enough.

138
00:12:47,570 --> 00:12:52,410
Clubs, networking, and academics.

139
00:12:55,770 --> 00:12:56,919
This is on the house.

140
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:59,070
But what my father really wanted...

141
00:12:59,730 --> 00:13:02,530
You must rank first in the school
on the next mock exam.

142
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:05,819
The only reason I let you dress like that

143
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:08,060
is because you said you'd do
what you're supposed to do.

144
00:13:08,490 --> 00:13:12,510
Wasn't for me to solve the endless
impossible tasks he threw at me...

145
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:22,510
Maybe he just wanted me to say
'I can't do it' and submit to him.

146
00:13:52,336 --> 00:13:54,463
[Goto Naoya's banking passbook]

147
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:27,320
For some reason,
I really want to see Takaaki right now.

148
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:34,700
(Incoming Call: Goto Naoya)

149
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:41,420
Hello.

150
00:14:41,530 --> 00:14:43,396
Ah, sorry for bothering
you while you're working.

151
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:44,420
Listen.

152
00:14:44,650 --> 00:14:46,260
Can I come over to your place today?

153
00:14:56,590 --> 00:14:57,590
Takaaki?

154
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:01,040
Got it.

155
00:15:02,990 --> 00:15:03,990
See you later then.

156
00:15:05,850 --> 00:15:06,990
Yeah.

157
00:15:21,890 --> 00:15:22,920
Excuse me.

158
00:15:25,283 --> 00:15:28,463
President, the documents you
asked for the other day are ready.

159
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,630
Thanks. Just leave them over there.

160
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:31,680
Understood.

161
00:15:31,970 --> 00:15:33,140
Um, President?

162
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:35,849
Sorry, cancel all my appointments
for the rest of the day.

163
00:15:35,850 --> 00:15:36,390
Huh?

164
00:15:36,391 --> 00:15:37,746
I'll leave the rescheduling to you.

165
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:38,889
- Ah...
- Good work.

166
00:15:38,890 --> 00:15:41,850
Good work...

167
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:51,660
How should I put this?
It's exactly as I imagined.

168
00:15:53,370 --> 00:15:54,370
Oh.

169
00:16:02,550 --> 00:16:03,550
Whoa.

170
00:16:04,010 --> 00:16:05,440
It's spotless.

171
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:07,380
Do you have a housekeeper?

172
00:16:07,490 --> 00:16:09,730
Yeah, I have someone
come clean once a week.

173
00:16:11,430 --> 00:16:16,950
And yet you still came to my
crappy apartment to clean and cook.

174
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:19,310
What's up with that?

175
00:16:20,430 --> 00:16:21,990
Why did you suddenly want to come over?

176
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:31,550
It feels like being forced to see
the gap between us.

177
00:16:36,030 --> 00:16:37,950
That's why I've always
been afraid to come here.

178
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:47,140
Actually, there's a coworker
named Mori-san at my part-time job.

179
00:16:50,590 --> 00:16:52,150
I think I mentioned him to you before.

180
00:16:52,350 --> 00:16:53,820
When I said I messed up at work.

181
00:16:57,010 --> 00:16:58,010
Yeah.

182
00:17:01,390 --> 00:17:02,390
Mori-san.

183
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:04,490
He helped me out a lot back then too.

184
00:17:05,020 --> 00:17:07,290
Afterward, the two of us talked for a bit.

185
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,880
We talked about my father.

186
00:17:11,710 --> 00:17:13,380
And my late mother.

187
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:18,660
About how much pressure
my father put on me.

188
00:17:19,330 --> 00:17:21,730
And how desperately I worked
just to keep from being crushed.

189
00:17:22,670 --> 00:17:25,580
But in the end, I still couldn't handle it.

190
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:33,440
Other than you, that was the first time
I've ever talked about myself like that.

191
00:17:36,090 --> 00:17:37,460
He listened to me so earnestly.

192
00:17:37,930 --> 00:17:39,050
And he accepted me.

193
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:41,600
If I had a son like you,

194
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:44,020
he would be my greatest pride.

195
00:17:48,350 --> 00:17:49,520
And then it hit me.

196
00:17:52,556 --> 00:17:55,436
I didn't want to become strong
like my father or you.

197
00:17:57,820 --> 00:18:03,300
I just wanted to live freely.
That's enough for me.

198
00:18:14,970 --> 00:18:19,470
Is this Mori-san more
'insignificant' than your father?

199
00:18:19,550 --> 00:18:21,510
No, why would you ask something like...

200
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:29,480
I guess so.

201
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:33,570
When it comes down to it,
what does it even mean to be 'strong'?

202
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:43,390
Naoya is turning over a new leaf
and rediscovering who he really is.

203
00:18:44,950 --> 00:18:46,750
He's found someone
who truly understands him.

204
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,330
He's expanding his horizons.

205
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:52,960
Even though for the longest time,
I was the only one by his side.

206
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:58,840
Takaaki?

207
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,460
That guy, Mori... How old is he?

208
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:08,330
He must be pushing sixty.

209
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:10,700
Looks like you've got pretty broad tastes.

210
00:19:11,310 --> 00:19:12,310
Excuse me?

211
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:13,920
What on earth are you talking about?

212
00:19:18,540 --> 00:19:20,199
Takaaki...

213
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,700
Stop it.

214
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:34,210
I get it.

215
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:39,840
Narrow-minded men like
me and Naoya's father...

216
00:20:41,150 --> 00:20:43,569
When it comes to the things we desire...

217
00:20:43,570 --> 00:20:46,880
If we can't control them and keep
them close, we're consumed by anxiety.

218
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:54,430
We let our desires imprison them.

219
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:58,840
We want to keep them caged up forever.

220
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:05,760
But...

221
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:10,310
I know that's wrong.

222
00:21:14,300 --> 00:21:15,300
That's why...

223
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:19,250
I've just been waiting for your orders.

224
00:21:21,940 --> 00:21:26,070
This guy... Since when
has he been thinking like this?

225
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:37,170
You're such an idiot.

226
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:41,730
How could you ever think
you're anything like that man?

227
00:21:44,550 --> 00:21:45,630
You know...

228
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:56,580
I really do care about you.

229
00:22:04,030 --> 00:22:07,820
When I lost all my pride, my
self-respect, and my social standing...

230
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:10,780
You were the only one
who stayed by my side.

231
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:20,980
Realizing I had to let you go
hurt more than anything else.

232
00:22:29,620 --> 00:22:31,600
Hey... Tell me.

233
00:22:33,260 --> 00:22:34,260
Tonight...

234
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:37,020
Do you want me?

235
00:22:55,780 --> 00:22:56,780
I want you.

236
00:23:02,070 --> 00:23:03,070
All right.

237
00:23:03,140 --> 00:23:04,140
Then take me.

238
00:24:22,300 --> 00:24:23,300
(Next Episode Preview)

239
00:24:23,390 --> 00:24:25,820
Next time you're in the mood,
just give me a call.

240
00:24:25,860 --> 00:24:27,810
The bathroom play costs extra, though.

241
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:30,479
The air in this room
is slowly filling with Naoya's scent.

242
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:32,639
Goto Construction reached out to see if I'd take
over as the head of the reconstruction project.

243
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:33,430
I turned them down.

244
00:24:33,431 --> 00:24:36,640
Just how much love has he poured
into silently watching over me?
